      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Myocardial infarction secondary to total obstruction of the left main coronary artery is an infrequent finding in clinical practice. Even though this disease usually results in high mortality rates, various cases have been described documenting survival after complete occlusion of the left main trunk. We present a patient who survived after a massive myocardial infarction due to total obstruction of the left main coronary artery. Orthotopic cardiac transplantation was subsequently performed with good results."},
